    {
      "id": "vblA",
      "code_hash": "03c4bdb05d7821f0a37a1dd5a9d95d9d",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"7-windows-and-asof-joins\">7. Windows and ASOF joins</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Say the maintenance team asks how long each sensor went quiet between\nreadings, because a long silence means a unit they should replace\nbefore it fails outright. For that you need, for every reading, the one\nbefore it.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Time-series pipelines constantly look at <em>neighbouring</em> rows like this:\nthe previous reading of the same sensor, the next event of the same\nuser, the position of a row within its group. SQL does this with\n<strong>window functions</strong>:</span>\n<div class=\"language-sql codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">LAG</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ts</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OVER</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">PARTITION</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">BY</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sensor</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">ORDER</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">BY</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ts</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">reads \"for each row, the <code>ts</code> of the previous row of the same sensor,\nin <code>ts</code> order\" (NULL for the first one). The model supports <code>LAG</code>,\n<code>LEAD</code> and <code>ROW_NUMBER</code>, with any sort directions, NULLs first or last,\noffsets and defaults (<code>SubstraitLean/Window.lean</code>).</span>\n<h2 id=\"lag-lead-and-row_number\">LAG, LEAD and ROW_NUMBER</h2></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
