          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Things to try:</span>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Lower the tolerance</strong> below 8 ms. The gyroscope samples every 7.7 ms,\n  so some accelerometer samples find no partner. With <code>how=\"left\"</code> they\n  stay, with NULLs; with <code>\"inner\"</code> they disappear. The proofs hold\n  either way.</li>\n<li><strong>Drop the key on <code>gyr</code>.</strong> Two gyroscope readings at the same instant\n  would tie for \"latest\", so the result is undetermined, and every\n  postcondition is refused (here as a warning, thanks to\n  <code>on_unproved=\"warn\"</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">One-row-per-sample comes from the key analysis: <code>ROW_NUMBER()</code> over a\npartition is a key together with the partition columns, and the filter\n<code>rank = 0</code> drops the rank from that key.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Windows are covered by contracts but <strong>not maintained incrementally</strong>\nyet: chapter 10 shows how a pipeline recomputes such views instead.\nFramed aggregates (<code>AVG(v) OVER (ROWS 5 PRECEDING)</code>), <code>RANK</code> and running\nsums are not supported yet.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">You can now prove facts about neighbouring rows, tell when ties leave a\nwindow's result up to the engine, and align two sensors with an ASOF\njoin that never reaches into the future. The maintenance team's gaps\nand the model's training pairs both rest on proofs. <strong>Next up:</strong>\n<a href=\"?file=08_composition.py\">Composing contracts</a>, where one step's\npromises become the next step's assumptions.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
